From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:43:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: drop a genfscon AOSP now declares itself

  genfs_contexts:1:ERROR 'duplicate entry for genfs entry
  (proc, /sys/vm/dirty_writeback_centisecs)'

system/sepolicy/private/genfs_contexts:88 labels it u:object_r:proc_dirty:s0,
which is exactly what this line said, so the device copy is now redundant
rather than wrong and the label does not change.

Swept the rest of the device's genfs_contexts against everything else in the
compiled policy set rather than waiting for checkpolicy to report the next
one: this was the only collision.

---
 sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
index 22022429..e45ec891 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
@@ -45,4 +45,3 @@ genfscon sysfs /devices/soc/400f000.qcom,spmi/spmi-0/spmi0-03/400f000.qcom,spmi:
 genfscon sysfs /devices/soc/74a4900.sdhci/leds                                                                                    u:object_r:sysfs_leds:s0
 
 # ProcFS
-genfscon proc /sys/vm/dirty_writeback_centisecs                     u:object_r:proc_dirty:s0
